@startuml
!include templates/plantuml-theme.puml

scale 2/3
center header
    C4 Architecture: Argo CD + Codefresh + Octopus — Release Flow (Dynamic / Level 4)
endheader

title Dynamic view — one release, end to end (who does what, in order)

actor "Developer /\nRelease Manager" as dev
participant "Octopus Deploy\n(orchestration + gates)" as oct
database "Azure SQL\n(app data + schema)" as sql
participant "Git Repo\n(desired state)" as git
participant "Argo CD Runtime\n(in-cluster reconciler)" as argo
participant "Codefresh\n(hosted Argo UI/health)" as cf
participant "K8s Cluster: k3s-in-WSL / AKS\n(runs the app)" as aks
participant "Container Registry\n(image store)" as acr

note over dev,acr
  Responsibilities: Octopus decides WHEN/WHETHER + runs migrations.
  Git is the source of truth. Argo does the actual cluster sync.
  Codefresh shows health. Nothing bypasses Git to touch the cluster.
end note

dev -> oct : 1. Create release, approve target environment
activate oct

oct -> sql : 2. Run DbUp migrations (schema first)
note right of sql : Schema owned by Octopus,\nNOT by Argo CD
sql --> oct : migrations applied

oct -> git : 3. Commit new image tag into deploy/overlays/dev
note right of git : This commit IS the deployment\n(history = deploy history)
git --> oct : commit pushed

argo -> git : 4. Detect changed desired state (poll/webhook)
activate argo
argo -> acr : 5. Resolve + pull the new image
acr --> argo : image ready
argo -> aks : 6. Apply Deployment; roll pods (respect probes)
aks --> argo : pods Ready on /_healthcheck
argo -> cf : 7. Report Synced + Healthy
deactivate argo

oct -> cf : 8. "Wait for Argo Application" polls status
cf --> oct : Synced + Healthy
note left of oct : Release GATE clears only\non real cluster health

oct --> dev : 9. Release succeeded (or promote to next env)
deactivate oct

FOOTER()
@enduml
